
  #90 -- locating the n=4000 recurrence ceiling (main sweep censored it at M=256)
  k=50 beta=0.1 p=0.05 buildT=6, chance floor 0.0125

       M   cover        engine       acc    ident   spread    secs
     256    3.20  numpy_sparse    1.0000   0.8962   0.0140    10.8
     256    3.20   numpy_exact    1.0000   0.9155   0.0147   215.8

     512    6.40  numpy_sparse    0.0078   0.2512   0.0795    24.4
     512    6.40   numpy_exact    0.0137   0.3382   0.1309  1265.7

  READING

    n=4000 rec ceiling on  numpy_sparse: M=256
    n=4000 rec ceiling on   numpy_exact: M=256

    Second clean step: n=2000 M=64 -> n=4000 M=256, 4.0x per doubling.
    First step was 16 -> 64, 4.0x. Two steps at ~4.0x and
    4.0x put the law near M_max ~ n^2, NOT M_max ~ n.

    Coverage at the ceiling: 3.20 here against 0.8
    at n=1000 -- rising with n, which a coverage law forbids.
    alpha* (1.15 n/k) predicts 92; measured 256.

    STILL ONLY THREE POINTS. An n^1.49 claim here was withdrawn
    once as an artifact; two clean steps are enough to say
    'super-linear, and not the stated law', and NOT enough to
    fit an exponent. The mechanism to test next is extreme-value
    statistics over n candidates -- an assembly survives its own
    recurrence while (1+beta)^T beats the max of n draws -- which
    predicts a ceiling growing faster than n and has nothing to
    do with coverage.
